WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:05.756
Kaleem clipped on Finn's leash, and they headed back to Troy's house.

2
00:00:05.757 --> 00:00:12.026
Daisy told Kaleem about Finn's problem.

3
00:00:12.027 --> 00:00:17.728
"Finn, are you sure Hazel stole your chew toy?" Daisy asked.

4
00:00:17.729 --> 00:00:21.931
"Yes! Hazel's owner doesn't let her leave toys in the yard.

5
00:00:21.932 --> 00:00:24.855
That's why I think she took mine."

6
00:00:24.856 --> 00:00:29.375
"We'll go ask her after we drop you off," Daisy said.

7
00:00:29.376 --> 00:00:31.648
"What does your missing toy look like?"

8
00:00:31.649 --> 00:00:35.430
"It's shaped like a doughnut," Finn said.

9
00:00:35.431 --> 00:00:39.341
"It squeaks when I bite it."

10
00:00:39.342 --> 00:00:41.286
Troy was waiting for them.

11
00:00:41.287 --> 00:00:47.909
He patted Finn and handed Daisy some money.

12
00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.987
"Thanks," he said.

13
00:00:50.988 --> 00:00:53.312
"Can you walk Finn again tomorrow?"

14
00:00:53.313 --> 00:00:57.166
"I'll come right after school. He's a great dog."

15
00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.405
Daisy gave Finn a hug.

16
00:00:59.406 --> 00:01:02.519
While she did, she whispered in his ear.

17
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.987
"We'll come back sooner if we find your chew toy."

18
00:01:05.988 --> 00:01:10.765
Finn wagged his tail. "I'll try not to chew anything until you find it.

19
00:01:10.766 --> 00:01:13.606
But I can't make any promises."

20
00:01:13.607 --> 00:01:17.257
Daisy just nodded and winked at him.

21
00:01:17.258 --> 00:01:24.778
She didn't want Troy to guess her secret.

22
00:01:24.779 --> 00:01:30.343
After Troy and Finn went inside, Daisy and Kaleem went next door.

23
00:01:30.344 --> 00:01:34.728
An old poodle was lying on the porch.

24
00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:38.755
"Hi, I'm Daisy. Are you Hazel?

25
00:01:38.756 --> 00:01:41.003
My friend Finn is missing a toy.

26
00:01:41.004 --> 00:01:44.877
It's shaped like a doughnut. Have you seen it?"

27
00:01:44.878 --> 00:01:48.784
The poodle sat up. "You're talking to me!"

28
00:01:48.785 --> 00:01:53.449
"Yes," Daisy said. "I can understand animals."

29
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:55.587
Hazel looked surprised.

30
00:01:55.588 --> 00:01:57.744
"Well, that's interesting.

31
00:01:57.745 --> 00:02:00.662
What were you saying about a doughnut?"

32
00:02:00.663 --> 00:02:09.576
Daisy explained again. When she finished, Hazel yawned.

33
00:02:09.577 --> 00:02:12.216
"I didn't take Finn's chew toy.

34
00:02:12.217 --> 00:02:16.238
I don't play with toys the way I did as a puppy.

35
00:02:16.239 --> 00:02:18.532
But I'm missing something too.

36
00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:22.140
My owner can't find my best sparkly collar.

37
00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:28.251
She left it on the porch yesterday, and it disappeared."

38
00:02:28.252 --> 00:02:34.490
Hazel wandered off to take a nap in the shade.

39
00:02:34.491 --> 00:02:38.713
Daisy told Kaleem about the poodle's missing collar.

40
00:02:38.714 --> 00:02:42.186
"This is sounding like a real mystery!"

41
00:02:42.187 --> 00:02:46.750
"Are you sure Hazel is telling the truth?" Kaleem asked.

42
00:02:46.751 --> 00:02:55.723
Beatrice had been sitting on Daisy's headband, but now she buzzed into the air.

43
00:02:55.724 --> 00:03:04.331
"Animals rarely lie. If Hazel says she didn't take Finn's toy, I believe her."

44
00:03:04.332 --> 00:03:10.838
"If animals don't lie, does that mean they don't steal, either?" Daisy asked.

45
00:03:10.839 --> 00:03:14.552
"No!" Kaleem laughed.

46
00:03:14.553 --> 00:03:18.117
"Dumpling stole a meatball off my plate last night."

47
00:03:18.118 --> 00:03:21.090
"The boy is right." Beatrice buzzed.

48
00:03:21.091 --> 00:03:25.994
"Animals take what they need, or sometimes just what they want.

49
00:03:25.995 --> 00:03:33.751
It's quite possible another dog took Finn's toy. But it wasn't Hazel."

50
00:03:33.752 --> 00:03:44.105
Daisy nodded. "Let's ask around."

51
00:03:44.106 --> 00:03:49.628
For the next half hour, Daisy talked to every dog she could find.

52
00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:52.307
She also talked to a few cats.

53
00:03:52.308 --> 00:03:57.835
None of them knew anything about Finn's toy.

54
00:03:57.836 --> 00:04:04.140
But a collie said her best tennis ball had gone missing.

55
00:04:04.141 --> 00:04:09.253
And one of the cats couldn't find his favorite catnip mouse.

56
00:04:09.254 --> 00:04:13.555
"I was playing with it a little while ago," the cat said.

57
00:04:13.556 --> 00:04:16.076
"I left it to chase a blowing leaf.

58
00:04:16.077 --> 00:04:21.241
When I came back, my mouse was gone."

59
00:04:21.242 --> 00:04:24.082
"Wow," Kaleem said.

60
00:04:24.083 --> 00:04:29.937
"It's a pet toy crime spree!"

